doc:sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20(7) Australian Federal Police and Other Legislation Amendment Act" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(7) If:  (a) the owner of a thing requests the return of the thing:  (i) within 90 days after the date of the seizure notice in relation to the thing; or  (ii) if subsection (2) applied in relation to the thing so that a seizure notice was not served—within 90 days after the seizure day; and  (b) the thing has not been returned to the owner by the end of the 90th day; the police officer who is for the time being responsible for the thing must, before the end of the 95th day:  (c) return the thing to the owner; or  (d) apply to a magistrate for an order under section 14M. Seizure day" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-federal-police-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2004-sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20(8) Australian Federal Police and Other Legislation Amendment Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20-2-ss-8 ;
    values:originalText "(8) In this section: seizure day means:  (a) in relation to a thing seized by a designated person who is a protective service officer—the day on which the thing was delivered into the custody of a police officer under subsection 14K(3); or  (b) in relation to a thing seized by a designated person who is a member or a special member—the day on which the thing was seized.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979" ;
    skos:definition "(8) In this section: seizure day means:  (a) in relation to a thing seized by a designated person who is a protective service officer—the day on which the thing was delivered into the custody of a police officer under subsection 14K(3); or  (b) in relation to a thing seized by a designated person who is a member or a special member—the day on which the thing was seized.  Schedule 1  Amendment of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5210fdcc251407e65d99028d8bc4c061bf531aaa563feb1a08f398eb8dd4df18" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-federal-police-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2004-sch-1-sec-20-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines seizure day for a thing seized by a designated person." ;
