concept:australian-federal-police-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2004-sch-3-sec-3aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3AA State offences that have a federal aspect"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-3aa ;
    values:originalText "Object  (1A) The object of this section is to identify State offences that have a federal aspect because:  (a) they potentially fall within Commonwealth legislative power because of the elements of the State offence; or  (b) they potentially fall within Commonwealth legislative power because of the circumstances in which the State offence was committed (whether or not those circumstances are expressed to be acts or omissions involved in committing the offence); or  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to the investigation of State offences that have a federal aspect" ;
    skos:definition "Object  (1A) The object of this section is to identify State offences that have a federal aspect because:  (a) they potentially fall within Commonwealth legislative power because of the elements of the State offence; or  (b) they potentially fall within Commonwealth legislative power because of the circumstances in which the State offence was committed (whether or not those circumstances are expressed to be acts or omissions involved in committing the offence); or  Schedule 3  Amendments relating to the investigation of State offences that have a federal aspect"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b145618f06db098a67300954dac35d1b466c1f4b0f84b70c636371f7c0a27eb6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "45"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Identify State offences with a federal aspect" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-federal-police-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2004.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-federal-police-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-2004.pdf, p.45" ;
